.TH ESS_COMPRESTIMATOR 1 "July 2026" "ess_comprestimator 2.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ess_comprestimator \- estimate FCM4 compression ratios for IBM Storage Scale (ESS/GPFS) data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ess_comprestimator
.BI \-\-path " PATH"
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ess_comprestimator
analyzes files under
.I PATH
and estimates the compression ratio that IBM Storage Scale Systems with
FCM4 drives would achieve on that data.
.PP
It samples files proportionally to their size, compresses 16 KB samples
with an algorithm similar to the FCM hardware compressor, and reports the
aggregate pre/post-compression sizes and the estimated ratio.
Already-compressed or encrypted data (for example
.BR .zip ", " .jpg ", " .mp4 )
is detected as incompressible, excluded from the estimate, and reported
separately.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p ", " \-\-path " PATH"
File or directory to analyze. Required.
.TP
.B \-\-exhaustive\-sample
Sample the entire data set. Most accurate, slowest.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-sampling\-percentage .
.TP
.BI \-\-sampling\-percentage " N"
Percentage of the data to sample, as an integer from 1 to 100.
Default: 10.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " PATTERN"
Exclude files or directories whose name matches the glob
.IR PATTERN .
May be given multiple times.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-hidden
Skip hidden files and directories (names starting with a dot).
.TP
.BI \-\-threads " N"
Number of parallel compression workers. Must be at least 1.
Default: the number of logical CPUs.
.TP
.BI \-l ", " \-\-error\-log " FILE"
Write the paths of files that could not be read or compressed to
.IR FILE .
Default:
.B comprestimator_errors.log
in the current directory.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
Progress is written to standard output while scanning and sampling.
On completion the tool prints the estimated compression ratio and the
pre- and post-compression sample sizes.
.PP
If some files could not be read, a
.B Note:
line reports how many were excluded from the estimate; the affected paths
are listed in the error log.
If part of the sampled data was incompressible, a further
.B Note:
line reports how much was excluded.
.PP
FCM4 drives are physically limited to 4x compression: if the estimate
exceeds 4x, provision vdisksets using 4x.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, unreadable path, or no data could be compressed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Estimate with the default 10% sample:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ess_comprestimator \-\-path /data/myvolume
.RE
.fi
.PP
Exhaustive scan skipping hidden files and logs:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ess_comprestimator \-\-path /data/myvolume \-\-exhaustive\-sample \\
    \-\-exclude\-hidden \-\-exclude "*.log"
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
Project home:
.UR https://github.com/cdmaestas/ess_comprestimator
.UE
